From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:42:05 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 276/297] Meridian: agent socket path stays short with a long
 profile path

A unix socket path must fit ~104 bytes. With a long profile folder (and a
long TMPDIR, where the fallback went) the socket couldn't be made and
the MCP bridge said "Meridian is not running". The socket now goes in
the profile folder when that fits, else /tmp/meridian-<uid>/<hash of the
profile path>.sock: a folder made 0700, checked to be this user's own
real folder (not a planted link), closed up if it was open. Clients
still find it in "Meridian Agent.json".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
